    "result_text": "Periods are in, and all 4 acceptance tests pass under `bin/e2e`.\n\n**What it does**\n- **Adding a period:** a new Periods section on the sheet has a form for a name and from/to dates. The server refuses a period that ends before it starts, reuses a name on the sheet, or overlaps another period. A refusal shows `period-form-error` and writes nothing.\n- **Audit line:** a period that goes through writes `PERIOD_ADDED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 period=<name> from=<date> to=<date>`.\n- **Claim's period:** each claim row shows `claim-period`, the name of the period whose dates include the claim's date, or empty if none does.\n- **Period due-total:** each `period-row-<name>` shows `period-due-total`, the sum of the dues of open and settled claims dated in that period. It's worked out on the screen the same way the person due-totals are, so it updates without reloading the sheet.\n\n**Two choices of mine you might want to check**\n- **Name matching ignores case.** \"p1\" counts as the same name as \"P1\", which is how person names already work. The test only tries an exact repeat.\n- **Claims with no due count as 0.** A counting claim with no rate for its date adds nothing to its period's due-total, rather than turning the total into \"n/a\".\n\n**Where the changes are**\n- **Server:**\n  - `V14__period.sql` adds the `period` table, with a unique name per sheet and a check that the from date is on or before the to date.\n  - The new `period/` package has the entity, repository, service and controller.\n  - Adding a period locks the sheet, so two people adding periods at once are checked one after the other.\n- **Front end:**\n  - `core/periods.service.ts` and `features/periods/periods.ts` are new.\n  - The sheet picker now loads periods with everything else and shows the new section.\n  - `person-claims.ts` has the claim-period cell.",
